I think that shopkeeper are far to easy to deal with.  In v3.0,
I would like to see several bugs (features) dealt with:

1) shopkeepers will not step on traps.  This means that they can not
chase you, or will get "stuck" somewhere.  This should be cleared up
before players are allowed to "set traps."

2) shopkeepers should get pissed off if you start setting traps in
their shops. (Wouldn't you?)

3) shopkeepers should only allow you to pick up so many items.  In other
words, you should not be able to pick up every scroll in the shop.  He
should not let you run up a bill you can't pay.

4) When you are invisable, you get to zap the shopkeepers at will.

5) You should not be able to repeatedly steal him blind, pay him a gold
piece, drop all you items, hide your gold, and do it again.

6) How about if the shopkeeper picks up all his items and stands on the
pile if you have worn out your welcome, with out getting him angry.
(lets say you dig a tunnel into a shop, so the shopkeeper picks everything
he can up before you can steal it)

7) Why not give a shopkeeper a random chance to have intrinsic teleport,
see invis, fire protection, esp, and/or cold protection.

8) My personal favorite way of disposing shopkeepers: Either #5, or
throw a potion of paralysis at him.  If I miss, he is not angry,
so I pick it up and throw it again.

Note: I've been playing enough version of nethack that I sometimes
get them mixed up, if some of these have been fixed, then opps.

And a Question: What good is a badge?

